<title>NETHERLANDS: Rabo Securities keeps Royal Dutch as a buy.</title>
<headline>Rabo Securities keeps Royal Dutch as a buy.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of February research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>Royal Dutch     Oil	     335     Rabo Securities</p>
<p>COMMENT: Buy. RD/Shell reported very good Q4 results. Despite share price rise, market has underestimated company's cost-cutting measures. Project stronger production growth in oil and gas. In chemicals, expect limited European growth and have lowered earnings estimates. Estimates based on Brent price of $19.88 (1997) and $18 (1998) and current exchange rates. In short, Royal Dutch is attractive long-term investment based on conservative expectations of oil and gas prices.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     16.31   20.5   9.4    10.55</p>
<p>    1997		  18.91   17.7   8.9    11.75</p>
<p>    1998		  20.27   16.5   8.3    13.00</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
